error[E0410]: `gone` is bound with `let`, so it cannot be assigned again
 --> mem:///main.lu:8:19
  |
6 |     let gone: int = 8
  |     --- the binding is made immutable here
7 |     match g(false) {
8 |         gone => { gone = 9 },
  |         ---- this pattern tests `gone` and binds nothing
  |                   ^^^^ this assignment needs a mutable binding
  |
  = note: `let` names a value once. Declare the binding with `var` to update it in place, or
    shadow it with a second `let` if the next value is really a new thing.
  = note: a bare name that spells a case of the scrutinee's type tests it and binds nothing, so
    inside its arm every name resolves as it does outside the `match`
    ([gram.pat.nullary.scope]).
help: make the binding mutable: `var`
  |
6 |     var gone: int = 8
  |
